  "title": "Erdős Problem #202",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $n_1<\\cdots < n_r\\leq N$ with associated $a_i\\pmod{n_i}$ such that the congruence classes are disjoint (that is, every integer is $\\equiv a_i\\pmod{n_i}$ for at most one $1\\leq i\\leq r$). How large can $r$ be in terms of $N$?",
